    "body": "\n\n## Overview\n\nPython's `SamplingParams.from_optional` clamps every `logit_bias` value to `[-100, 100]` for every entry point, so a bias of `250` behaves like `100`. The Rust frontend forwards the value to the engine unchanged, so the same request samples differently on the two frontends. This PR clamps biases in `vllm_text::lower_sampling_params`.\n\nSupersedes the inactive draft vllm-project/vllm#50350, which clamps in the HTTP-only `convert_logit_bias` helper.\n\n## Claims\n\n- Rust clamps each `logit_bias` value to `[-100, 100]` before it reaches engine-core, matching `SamplingParams.from_optional`.\n- The clamp applies to every Rust entry point: `/v1/chat/completions`, `/v1/completions`, `/inference/v1/generate`, and gRPC.\n- In-range values are unchanged; key parsing and the out-of-vocab check are unchanged.\n\n## Validation\n\nCommands from `.buildkite/scripts/run-rust-frontend-cargo-ci.sh` (`style-clippy` and `test` modes), run from the repo root:\n\n```\ncargo fmt --manifest-path rust/Cargo.toml --all -- --check   # ok\ncargo sort --workspace --check rust                          # ok\ncargo deny --manifest-path rust/Cargo.toml --config rust/deny.toml check bans   # ok\ncargo clippy --manifest-path rust/Cargo.toml --workspace --all-targets --all-features --locked -- -D warnings   # ok\ncargo nextest run --manifest-path rust/Cargo.toml --workspace --all-features --locked --no-fail-fast\n# 2140 tests run: 2140 passed, 13 skipped\n```\n\nNew test: `vllm-text` `lower_sampling_params_clamps_logit_bias` (`{5: 250, 6: -300, 7: 1.5}` lowers to `{5: 100, 6: -100, 7: 1.5}`). With the fix reverted and the test kept, it fails: `left: Some({6: -300.0, 5: 250.0, 7: 1.5})`.\n\n## Details\n\n- **Where the clamp lives.** `vllm_text::lower_sampling_params` turns northbound sampling params into engine-core params, and every Rust entry point goes through it. Python clamps at the equivalent point, `SamplingParams` construction. Clamping in `convert_logit_bias` 